IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `act-ch1-preliminary`
IMPORT `act-ch13-structure`
IMPORT `act-ch15-aids`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person who has a time limit to meet under an ACT Act or subordinate law (to apply, object, appeal, reply or pay),
-- or who needs to know when something takes effect, asking on which day their period ends and which of their days count.
--
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person asks.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the module's inputs from plain answers and calls the module's rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS. Every question takes plain inputs: yes or no, a number, a date, or one of the modules' own short lists of choices.
-- Where a module takes an optional value, the question asks "is there one?" and "what is it?" as two inputs and builds the optional value inside.
-- A date that is asked only when the answer to the yes-or-no input before it is yes is given any date otherwise; the question says so.
--
-- WHAT THE ANSWERS LEAVE OUT (stated here once; NOTES.md repeats it).
--   * A day is asked as a day. The time of day within it is not asked: a commencement the law fixes at a stated time is entered as that day, and is read as the start of the day.
--   * The Holidays Act is not among the sources, so public holidays, bank holidays and days an office is closed are asked as up to three days "that do not count".
--     They are used for all three purposes at once; whichever of the three the thing to be done needs is the one the module looks at.
--     For something done at an office, a day is a working day when the office is open, so Saturdays and Sundays on which it is closed must be listed among the three days too.
--     If more than three days in a row do not count, the answer may be a day that does not count.
--   * Whether s 151 and s 151A apply to a law enacted or made on or before 1 January 2006, and what a contrary intention does to them, is worked out from three yes-or-no answers (the module's s 6 rule).
--     A provision inserted after that date into an older law is not asked.
--   * Where an answer is NOTHING, the text does not answer the question for the facts given. That is the normal "not covered" value of every module.
--
-- The questions follow the order of the Act: when a law begins (chapter 8), when it ends (chapter 9),
-- ages, periods and fines (chapters 13 and 15), and documents served on the person (chapter 19).

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT) -- the questions of a person with a time limit`

§§ `When an Act or instrument that affects me begins`

-- ss 73 (1), 74 (1). An Act begins on the day the Act, or another Act, says; if none says, at the start of the day after it is notified.
@export On which day does an Act begin (ss 73 (1), 74 (1))?
GIVEN `the day the Act was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the Act notified on the ACT legislation register?
      `the Act, or another Act, says when the Act begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act itself, or another Act, say on which day the Act begins?
      `the day the Act says it begins` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it say the Act begins? (Give any date if it does not say.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an Act begin` IS
    `the commencement`'s `day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement` MEANS `s 73 (1) and s 74 (1): when an Act commences` `the day the Act was notified` `the commencement provided`
        `the commencement provided` MEANS
            IF   `the Act, or another Act, says when the Act begins`
            THEN JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day the Act says it begins`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- ss 73 (2), (3). A legislative instrument begins at the start of the day after it is notified, unless a provision gives a later or earlier time.
@export On which day does a legislative instrument begin (ss 73 (2), (3))?
GIVEN `the day the instrument was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the instrument notified on the ACT legislation register?
      `the instrument says when it begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument, or an Act, say on which day the instrument begins?
      `the day it says it begins` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it say the instrument begins? (Give any date if it does not say.)
      `who provides that day` IS A `Who provides a commencement` @desc Who provides that day: an Act, the instrument without authority given by an Act, or the instrument under authority given by an Act? (Choose any if no day is stated.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a legislative instrument begin` IS
    `the commencement`'s `day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement` MEANS `s 73 (2) and (3): when a legislative instrument commences` `the day the instrument was notified` `the commencement provided` `who provides that day`
        `the commencement provided` MEANS
            IF   `the instrument says when it begins`
            THEN JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day it says it begins`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 73 (4). An instrument that is not a legislative instrument begins at the start of the day after it is made or, if it must be approved, approved.
@export On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin (s 73 (4))?
GIVEN `the day the instrument was made` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the instrument made?
      `the instrument must be approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must the instrument be approved before it takes effect?
      `the day the instrument was approved` IS A DATE @desc If it must be approved, on which day was it approved? (Give any date if approval is not required.)
      `the instrument says when it begins` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the instrument, or an Act, say on which day the instrument begins?
      `the day it says it begins` IS A DATE @desc On which day does it say the instrument begins? (Give any date if it does not say.)
      `who provides that day` IS A `Who provides a commencement` @desc Who provides that day: an Act, the instrument without authority given by an Act, or the instrument under authority given by an Act? (Choose any if no day is stated.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does an instrument that is not a legislative instrument begin` IS
    `the commencement`'s `day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement` MEANS `s 73 (4): when a statutory instrument that is not a legislative instrument commences` `the day the instrument was made` `the day approved, if approval is required` `the commencement provided` `who provides that day`
        `the day approved, if approval is required` MEANS
            IF   `the instrument must be approved`
            THEN JUST `the day the instrument was approved`
            ELSE NOTHING
        `the commencement provided` MEANS
            IF   `the instrument says when it begins`
            THEN JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day it says it begins`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 75A (1). A law begins retrospectively if it begins before the day it was notified.
@export Does a law begin before the day it was notified (s 75A (1))?
GIVEN `the day the law was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the Act or legislative instrument notified?
      `the day the law begins` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the law begin?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a law begin before the day it was notified` IS
    `s 75A (1): an Act or legislative instrument commences retrospectively` `the day the law was notified` (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day the law begins`)

-- ss 77 (3), (4). A commencement notice cannot fix a day before its own notification day unless it clearly says so under authority given by an Act.
@export On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice (ss 77 (3), (4))?
GIVEN `the day the notice fixes` IS A DATE @desc Which day does the commencement notice fix for the law to begin?
      `the day the notice was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the commencement notice itself notified?
      `the notice clearly says the law begins earlier, under authority given by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice clearly say that the law begins on an earlier day, under authority given by an Act?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a law begin under a commencement notice` IS
    `the commencement`'s `day`
    WHERE
        `the commencement` MEANS
            `s 77 (3), (4): when a law commences under a commencement notice`
                (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day the notice fixes`)
                `the day the notice was notified`
                `the notice clearly says the law begins earlier, under authority given by an Act`

-- s 79 (1). A law whose commencement was postponed by a commencement notice begins on its own if it has not begun within 6 months of its notification day.
@export On which day does a postponed law begin by itself (s 79 (1))?
GIVEN `the day the law was notified` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the law notified?
      `the law has begun within the 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the law already begun within the 6 months starting on the day it was notified?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does a postponed law begin by itself` IS
    CONSIDER `s 79 (1): when a postponed law automatically commences` `the day the law was notified` `the law has begun within the 6 months`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST point THEN JUST (point's `day`)

§§ `When a law that affects me ends`

-- Situation: a law has been repealed, or is an amending law or appropriation Act that ends by itself.
-- s 85. The repeal of a law takes effect at the end of the day of repeal, unless the law is remade that day, when it takes effect as the remade law begins.
@export On which day does the repeal of a law take effect (s 85)?
GIVEN `the day the law is repealed` IS A DATE @desc On which day is the law repealed?
      `the law is remade on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the law remade on the day it is repealed?
      `the remade law begins on a stated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is remade, does the remade law say on which day it begins?
      `the day the remade law begins` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the remade law begin? (Give any date if it is not remade or does not say.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does the repeal of a law take effect` IS
    CONSIDER `s 85: when the repeal of a law takes effect` `the day the law is repealed` `the law is remade on that day` `the commencement of the remade law`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST point THEN JUST (point's `day`)
    WHERE
        `the commencement of the remade law` MEANS
            IF   `the remade law begins on a stated day`
            THEN JUST (`s 74 (1), (2): the beginning of a day` `the day the remade law begins`)
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 89 (1). An amending law is repealed on the day after the earlier of the day all its provisions have begun and the day the last provisions that have not begun were omitted or could not begin.
@export On which day is an amending law repealed by itself (s 89 (1))?
GIVEN `all its provisions have begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all the provisions of the amending law begun?
      `the day all its provisions had begun` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day had they all begun? (Give any date if not.)
      `the last provisions that had not begun were omitted or could not begin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the provisions that had not begun omitted, or did it become impossible for them to begin?
      `the day they were omitted or could not begin` IS A DATE @desc If so, on which day? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day is an amending law repealed by itself` IS
    `s 89 (1): the day an amending law is automatically repealed` `the first day` `the second day`
    WHERE
        `the first day` MEANS
            IF   `all its provisions have begun`
            THEN JUST `the day all its provisions had begun`
            ELSE NOTHING
        `the second day` MEANS
            IF   `the last provisions that had not begun were omitted or could not begin`
            THEN JUST `the day they were omitted or could not begin`
            ELSE NOTHING

-- s 89 (2). An appropriation Act is repealed at the end of the financial year, 12 months from 1 July of the calendar year in which the financial year begins.
@export On which day is an appropriation Act repealed by itself (s 89 (2))?
GIVEN `the calendar year in which the financial year begins` IS A NUMBER @desc In which calendar year does the financial year begin? (For the financial year starting 1 July 2025, enter 2025.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On which day is an appropriation Act repealed by itself` IS
    `s 89 (2): the day an appropriation Act is automatically repealed` `the calendar year in which the financial year begins`

§§ `Ages and periods of time`

-- s 149. A person is an age in years at the beginning of the person's birthday for the age.
@export How old am I on a given day (s 149)?
GIVEN `the day I was born` IS A DATE @desc On which day were you born?
      `the day I want to know my age on` IS A DATE @desc On which day do you want to know your age?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How old am I on a given day` IS
    `s 149: the age in years of a person on a day` `the day I was born` `the day I want to know my age on`

-- s 149.
@export On which day do I reach a given age (s 149)?
GIVEN `the day I was born` IS A DATE @desc On which day were you born?
      `the age` IS A NUMBER @desc Which age, in years, do you want to know the day for?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day do I reach a given age` IS
    `s 149: the day a person attains an age in years` `the day I was born` `the age`

-- s 151 (2), table 151. How the period is described decides whether the stated day is counted.
@export Is the day my period is counted from or to part of the period (s 151 (2), table 151)?
GIVEN `how my period is described` IS A `How a period is described` @desc How does the law describe your period: beginning at, on or with a day; beginning from or after a day; ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a day; ending before a day; or occurring between 2 events?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the day my period is counted from or to part of the period` IS
    `s 151 (2), table 151: the period includes the stated day` `how my period is described`

-- s 151 (3). If something may be done within a period after a stated day, it may be done on the stated day.
@export May I act on the day my period is counted from (s 151 (3))?
GIVEN `how my period is described` IS A `How a period is described` @desc How does the law describe your period: beginning at, on or with a day; beginning from or after a day; ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a day; ending before a day; or occurring between 2 events?
      `the law says I may act within a period of time after the stated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law say that you may or must act within a period of time after the stated day?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I act on the day my period is counted from` IS
    `s 151 (3): the thing may be done on the stated day` `how my period is described` `the law says I may act within a period of time after the stated day`

-- s 151 (1), (2), table 151, and the dictionary definitions of month and year. The last day of a period of days, months or years.
-- s 151 and s 6. If the law that sets the period says something different about how periods are counted, the Act does not answer.
@export On which day does my period end (s 151, dictionary: month, year)?
GIVEN `the number in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days, weeks, months or years is your period? (Give the number only.)
      `the unit of my period` IS A `Unit of time` @desc Is your period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is described` IS A `How a period is described` @desc How does the law describe your period: beginning at, on or with a day; beginning from or after a day; ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a day; ending before a day; or occurring between 2 events?
      `the stated day` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the period is counted from (for example, the day you were given a notice)?
      `the day the law was enacted or made` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the Act enacted or the subordinate law or instrument made?
      `the law says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that sets your period say expressly that the Legislation Act's way of counting periods does not apply?
      `the law shows a different intention about counting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that sets your period show an intention that periods be counted differently?
      `that different intention is clear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that intention clear (manifest) from the law?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day does my period end` IS
    CONSIDER `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `the displacement facts`
    WHEN JUST displaced THEN
        IF   displaced
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` `the number in my period` `the unit of my period` `how my period is described` `the stated day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` `the number in my period` `the unit of my period` `how my period is described` `the stated day`
    WHERE
        `the displacement facts` MEANS `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
            `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS `s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `the day the law was enacted or made` NOTHING
            `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS `the law says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply`
            `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS `the law shows a different intention about counting`
            `the contrary intention is manifest` IS `that different intention is clear`
            -- Placeholder: asked of nobody; the two provisions are taken not to operate together once the law says something different.
            `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the only ground (that both deal with the same subject) is not what the person is asked about.
            `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE

-- s 151A (4). A day is a working day or not according to what is to be done.
@export Is a day a working day for what I must do (s 151A (4))?
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE @desc Which day do you want to check?
      `what I must do` IS A `What is to be done` @desc What must or may you do: something at an office of a court, tribunal, government unit or other public body; something else; or something else by or in relation to a bank or other deposit-taking institution?
      `there is a first day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday (or bank holiday, or a day the office is closed, including a Saturday or Sunday if you must act at an office) that you want counted as a day that does not count?
      `the first day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second such day?
      `the second day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `there is a third day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a third such day?
      `the third day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is a day a working day for what I must do` IS
    `s 151A (4): the day is a working day for doing the thing` `the day` `what I must do` `the calendar`
    WHERE
        `the calendar` MEANS `Calendar facts` WITH
            `public holidays` IS `the days that do not count`
            `bank holidays` IS `the days that do not count`
            `days when the office is not open` IS `the days that do not count`
        `the days that do not count` MEANS
            append
                (IF `there is a first day that does not count` THEN LIST `the first day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY)
                (append
                    (IF `there is a second day that does not count` THEN LIST `the second day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY)
                    (IF `there is a third day that does not count` THEN LIST `the third day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY))

-- ss 151, 151A. The last day of the period moves to the next working day when it is not one.
@export By which day must I act (ss 151, 151A)?
GIVEN `the number in my period` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days, weeks, months or years is your period? (Give the number only.)
      `the unit of my period` IS A `Unit of time` @desc Is your period counted in days, weeks, months or years?
      `how my period is described` IS A `How a period is described` @desc How does the law describe your period: beginning at, on or with a day; beginning from or after a day; ending at, by, on or with, or continuing to or until, a day; ending before a day; or occurring between 2 events?
      `the stated day` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the period is counted from (for example, the day you were given a notice)?
      `what I must do` IS A `What is to be done` @desc What must or may you do: something at an office of a court, tribunal, government unit or other public body; something else; or something else by or in relation to a bank or other deposit-taking institution?
      `there is a first day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a public holiday (or bank holiday, or a day the office is closed, including a Saturday or Sunday if you must act at an office) just after the day your period would otherwise end?
      `the first day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `there is a second day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a second such day?
      `the second day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `there is a third day that does not count` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there a third such day?
      `the third day that does not count` IS A DATE @desc Which day is it? (Give any date if there is none.)
      `the day the law was enacted or made` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the Act enacted or the subordinate law or instrument made?
      `the law says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that sets your period say expressly that the Legislation Act's way of counting periods or of moving a last day does not apply?
      `the law shows a different intention about counting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law that sets your period show an intention that periods be counted, or a last day be moved, differently?
      `that different intention is clear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, is that intention clear (manifest) from the law?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `By which day must I act` IS
    CONSIDER `s 6: the provision of this Act is displaced by the other provision` `the displacement facts`
    WHEN JUST displaced THEN
        IF   displaced
        THEN NOTHING
        ELSE `the answer under sections 151 and 151A`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the answer under sections 151 and 151A`
    WHERE
        `the answer under sections 151 and 151A` MEANS
            `s 151 and s 151A: the last day on which the thing may be done within a period that begins on or from a stated day`
                `the number in my period` `the unit of my period` `how my period is described` `the stated day` `what I must do` `the calendar`
        `the displacement facts` MEANS `Facts about a possible displacement` WITH
            `the provision of this Act is a determinative provision` IS `s 151 (5), s 151A (4), s 151C (6): the law or the provision is an applicable law or applicable provision` `the day the law was enacted or made` NOTHING
            `the other provision expressly displaces it` IS `the law says expressly that this Act's counting does not apply`
            `the other provision shows a contrary intention` IS `the law shows a different intention about counting`
            `the contrary intention is manifest` IS `that different intention is clear`
            -- Placeholder: asked of nobody; the two provisions are taken not to operate together once the law says something different.
            `the two provisions can operate concurrently` IS FALSE
            -- Placeholder: the only ground (that both deal with the same subject) is not what the person is asked about.
            `the only ground is that the two provisions deal with the same or a similar subject matter` IS FALSE
        `the calendar` MEANS `Calendar facts` WITH
            `public holidays` IS `the days that do not count`
            `bank holidays` IS `the days that do not count`
            `days when the office is not open` IS `the days that do not count`
        `the days that do not count` MEANS
            append
                (IF `there is a first day that does not count` THEN LIST `the first day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY)
                (append
                    (IF `there is a second day that does not count` THEN LIST `the second day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY)
                    (IF `there is a third day that does not count` THEN LIST `the third day that does not count` ELSE EMPTY))

-- s 151 (2), table 151, item 5. A period between 2 events does not include the days of the events.
@export What is the latest day for the earlier event, so that a number of days lie between 2 events (s 151 (2), table 151 item 5)?
GIVEN `the number of days that must lie between` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days must lie between the two events?
      `the day of the later event` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the later event happen (for example, the hearing)?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the latest day for the earlier event` IS
    `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the latest day for the earlier event, so that the given number of days lie between the 2 events` `the number of days that must lie between` `the day of the later event`

-- s 151 (2), table 151, item 5.
@export How many days lie between 2 events (s 151 (2), table 151 item 5)?
GIVEN `the day of the earlier event` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the earlier event happen?
      `the day of the later event` IS A DATE @desc On which day does the later event happen?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days lie between 2 events` IS
    `s 151 (2), table 151 item 5: the number of days between 2 events` `the day of the earlier event` `the day of the later event`

-- s 151B. A thing for which the law fixes no time must or may be done as soon as possible and as often as needed.
@export When must I do something for which the law sets no time (s 151B)?
GIVEN `the law says I must or may do the thing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an Act or subordinate law say that you must or may do the thing?
      `the law sets no time for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law set no time for doing it?
GIVETH A MAYBE `When a thing with no fixed time must or may be done`
DECIDE `When must I do something for which the law sets no time` IS
    `s 151B (2): when the thing must or may be done` (`s 151B (1): s 151B applies to the thing` `the law says I must or may do the thing` `the law sets no time for it`)

-- s 151C. A person may apply to extend a time even though it has ended, where a court or other entity can extend it.
@export May I ask for more time even though my time has ended (s 151C)?
GIVEN `the day the law was enacted or made` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the Act enacted or the subordinate law or instrument made?
      `I must or may act on a day or within a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Must or may you act on a particular day or within a period of time?
      `a court or other body can extend the time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a court or other body have power to extend the time for acting?
      `my time has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your time already ended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for more time even though my time has ended` IS
    IF   `s 151C (5): s 151C applies to the law or provision` `the day the law was enacted or made` NOTHING
    THEN `s 151C (2): a person may apply for the relevant time to be extended` (`s 151C (1): s 151C applies to the thing` `I must or may act on a day or within a period` `a court or other body can extend the time`) `my time has ended`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 152. The obligation to do an act continues until it is done, even after the time for it has passed.
@export Must I still do what the law requires after the time for it has passed (s 152)?
GIVEN `a provision requires me to do the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a provision of an Act or subordinate law require you to do the act?
      `I have done the act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you done the act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I still do what the law requires after the time for it has passed` IS
    `s 152: the obligation to do the act continues` `a provision requires me to do the act` `I have done the act`

§§ `Fines I must pay`

-- Situation: a fine is expressed in penalty units.
-- s 133 (1), (2). A penalty of a number of penalty units is a fine of that number of units; a unit is $160 for an individual and $810 for a corporation.
@export How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars (s 133 (1), (2))?
GIVEN `the kind of law that sets the penalty` IS A `Kind of Act or instrument` @desc Is the penalty set by an Act, a subordinate law, a disallowable instrument, a notifiable instrument, a commencement notice or another statutory instrument?
      `the offender` IS A `Kind of offender` @desc Is the offence committed by an individual, by a corporation, or by neither?
      `the penalty is a number of penalty units` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law express the penalty as a number of penalty units?
      `the number of penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc How many penalty units? (A fraction is allowed. Give 0 if the penalty is not in penalty units.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is a fine expressed in penalty units, in dollars` IS
    `s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` `the kind of law that sets the penalty` `the offender` `the penalty is a number of penalty units` `the number of penalty units`

-- s 161 (3). Where a law gives only a period of imprisonment, a corporation convicted of the offence faces a fine in penalty units set by the period.
@export What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment (s 161 (3))?
GIVEN `the corporation is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been convicted of the offence?
      `the penalty is imprisonment only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the law set only a period of imprisonment as the penalty?
      `the months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months of imprisonment does the law set? (A year is 12 months; 2 years is 24.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most a corporation can be fined where the law sets only imprisonment` IS
    `s 161 (3): the most the court may impose on the corporation, in penalty units` `the corporation is convicted` `the penalty is imprisonment only` `the months of imprisonment`

§§ `Documents served on me`

-- Situation: a document has been or is to be served on the person.
-- s 250. A document is taken to be served on the day it would arrive by post, or on the day it is sent by fax or email, or left at an address.
@export On which day am I taken to be served (s 250)?
GIVEN `how the document was served` IS A `How a document is served` @desc How was the document served: by giving it to you or an executive officer; by prepaid post; by fax; by email; or by leaving it at an address with someone there?
      `the day it was posted, sent or left` IS A DATE @desc On which day was the document posted, sent or left?
      `the day it would have arrived in the ordinary course of post` IS A DATE @desc If it was posted, on which day would it have been delivered in the ordinary course of post? (Give any date if it was not posted.)
      `the equipment indicated a failure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it was sent by fax or email, did the sender's equipment indicate a failure on the day it was sent or the next working day? (No if it was not sent that way.)
      `evidence raising doubt is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there evidence enough to raise doubt that the document was served on that day?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `On which day am I taken to be served` IS
    `s 250: the day a document is taken to be served`
        `how the document was served`
        `the day it was posted, sent or left`
        (JUST `the day it would have arrived in the ordinary course of post`)
        (`s 250 (4): the sender has reason to suspect the document was not received` `the equipment indicated a failure`)
        `evidence raising doubt is given`
